{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "9004db7c-8bdf-5c53-a892-e92c30054132",
    "name": "Querylab API (step 0)",
    "description": "Every endpoint the backend has after step 0: health, the current user, and allauth's headless (browser) API. Sign-in is Google or GitHub only.\n\n**Setup:** import this collection and `environment.json`, select the *Querylab local* environment,\n\n**CSRF:** run *Get CSRF cookie and current user* first. A collection test script copies the `csrftoken` cookie into `{{csrfToken}}` after every response (Django rotates it at login), and a collection pre-request script sends it as `X-CSRFToken` on every write.\n\n**Responses:** `/api/*` uses Querylab's envelope (`success`, `data`, ...; `/api/health` is unwrapped). `/_allauth/*` uses allauth's own shape (`status`, `data`, `meta`).",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "prerequest",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// Send the CSRF token on every write (Django checks it on POST/PUT/PATCH/DELETE).",
          "const unsafe = ['POST', 'PUT', 'PATCH', 'DELETE'];",
          "const token = pm.environment.get('csrfToken');",
          "if (unsafe.includes(pm.request.method) && token) {",
          "  pm.request.headers.upsert({ key: 'X-CSRFToken', value: token });",
          "}"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "listen": "test",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// Keep {{csrfToken}} in step with the csrftoken cookie (it rotates at login).",
          "const cookie = pm.cookies.get('csrftoken');",
          "if (cookie) pm.environment.set('csrfToken', cookie);"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "1. Health and docs",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Health",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/health",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "health"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Every backend dependency: `querylab_app`, `querylab`, the read-only reader, Redis and the Huey worker. 200 with `status: ok`, or 503 with `status: degraded` and the failing check marked `fail`. Not wrapped in the envelope."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is one of [200, 503]', () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.be.oneOf([200, 503]));",
                  "pm.test('reports every check', () => {",
                  "  const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.have.keys('status', 'app_db', 'data_db', 'data_reader', 'redis', 'worker');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "OpenAPI schema",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/openapi.json",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "openapi.json"
              ]
            },
            "description": "The generated OpenAPI document for `/api/` (the interactive docs are at `/api/docs` in a browser)."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is one of [200]', () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.be.oneOf([200]));",
                  "pm.test('is OpenAPI', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json()).to.have.property('openapi'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "2. Current user",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Get CSRF cookie and current user (GET /api/me)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/me",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "me"
              ]
            },
            "description": "**Run this first.** Returns the signed-in user (200, envelope, with `providers`: `google` or `github`) or 401 when signed out. Either way it sets the `csrftoken` cookie, which the collection copies into `{{csrfToken}}` for every write."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is one of [200, 401]', () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.be.oneOf([200, 401]));",
                  "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
                  "  pm.test('success envelope', () => {",
                  "    const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(body.success).to.equal(true);",
                  "    pm.expect(body).to.have.property('data');",
                  "  });",
                  "  pm.test('returns the user', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().data).to.include.keys('id', 'email'));",
                  "} else {",
                  "  pm.test('error envelope', () => {",
                  "    const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(body.success).to.equal(false);",
                  "    pm.expect(body).to.have.keys('success', 'status_code', 'message', 'code', 'errors');",
                  "  });",
                  "}",
                  "pm.test('csrftoken cookie is set', () => pm.expect(pm.cookies.has('csrftoken')).to.equal(true));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "3. Sign in with Google or GitHub (finish in a browser)",
      "description": "Querylab has no email/password accounts. Start the redirect here, finish the provider's consent in a browser, then copy the session cookie into Postman to call the signed-in requests.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Config",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/_allauth/browser/v1/config",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "_allauth",
                "browser",
                "v1",
                "config"
              ]
            },
            "description": "What allauth allows: no local login or signup (social-only), and the configured providers (Google, GitHub)."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is one of [200]', () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.be.oneOf([200]));",
                  "pm.test('allauth response shape', () => {",
                  "  const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property('status', pm.response.code);",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('offers Google and GitHub', () => {",
                  "  const ids = pm.response.json().data.socialaccount.providers.map((p) => p.id);",
                  "  pm.expect(ids).to.have.members(['google', 'github']);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Start Google sign-in",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "body": {
              "mode": "urlencoded",
              "urlencoded": [
                {
                  "key": "provider",
                  "value": "google"
                },
                {
                  "key": "process",
                  "value": "login"
                },
                {
                  "key": "callback_url",
                  "value": "{{frontendUrl}}/auth/callback"
                },
                {
                  "key": "csrfmiddlewaretoken",
                  "value": "{{csrfToken}}"
                }
              ]
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/_allauth/browser/v1/auth/provider/redirect",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "_allauth",
                "browser",
                "v1",
                "auth",
                "provider",
                "redirect"
              ]
            },
            "description": "The only way to sign in. A form POST that answers with a redirect to Google; the OAuth flow can only finish in a browser. With placeholder client ids, the provider's own error page is the expected result. Turn off 'Automatically follow redirects' to see the 302."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is one of [302, 200]', () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.be.oneOf([302, 200]));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Start GitHub sign-in",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "body": {
              "mode": "urlencoded",
              "urlencoded": [
                {
                  "key": "provider",
                  "value": "github"
                },
                {
                  "key": "process",
                  "value": "login"
                },
                {
                  "key": "callback_url",
                  "value": "{{frontendUrl}}/auth/callback"
                },
                {
                  "key": "csrfmiddlewaretoken",
                  "value": "{{csrfToken}}"
                }
              ]
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/_allauth/browser/v1/auth/provider/redirect",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "_allauth",
                "browser",
                "v1",
                "auth",
                "provider",
                "redirect"
              ]
            },
            "description": "The only way to sign in. A form POST that answers with a redirect to GitHub; the OAuth flow can only finish in a browser. With placeholder client ids, the provider's own error page is the expected result. Turn off 'Automatically follow redirects' to see the 302."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is one of [302, 200]', () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.be.oneOf([302, 200]));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "4. Session (signed in)",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Session",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/_allauth/browser/v1/auth/session",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "_allauth",
                "browser",
                "v1",
                "auth",
                "session"
              ]
            },
            "description": "The current session: 200 with the user when signed in (after a Google or GitHub sign-in in the same cookie jar), 401 when signed out."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is one of [200, 401]', () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.be.oneOf([200, 401]));",
                  "pm.test('allauth response shape', () => {",
                  "  const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property('status', pm.response.code);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Connected providers",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/_allauth/browser/v1/account/providers",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
